# Client (Vite dev server and Playwright) settings. Both are optional; the defaults work with the local setup.
# Placeholders only. Every variable is described in docs/labs/lab-05/deployment.md.

# Where the Vite dev server proxies /api (default http://localhost:3000). Not used in the cloud, where the API
# container serves the built client itself.
# API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:3000

# GitHub Actions sets CI itself. When it is set, Playwright starts its own dev server instead of reusing one that
# is already running. Leave it unset on your computer.
# CI=

# The commit the UI was built from, shown in the footer as "Build <first 7 characters>" (F-05 v0.10). The Docker
# build sets it from the build argument GIT_SHA, and the deploy workflow passes the commit SHA. Unset gives "Build dev".
# Not a secret.
# VITE_GIT_SHA=
